# chatter: chat sessions told with source "chat" (user turns only, as an MCP client relays them). A task only for the user's own commitment; off-topic chat (coding help, a recipe, an assistant's advice, a friend's task) makes none. All cases are fictional, written to read like real chats; noise-coding is the kind of long coding chat that once made two tasks. Runs the REAL tiers: `ken eval reconcile evals/chatter.jsonl`.
{"id": "real-plumber", "source": "chat", "seed": {}, "report": "User: Quick update on the kitchen. I need to call Tomas the plumber on Friday to confirm the start date.", "expect": {"must": {"add_task": ["task", "task_exists", "pending"]}}}
